Build-environment notes (not part of the Arrow patch):
  The host's /usr/local/include holds x86_64 Homebrew protobuf 29.3, abseil, c-ares and utf8_range
  headers, and Apple clang searches it ahead of the bundled -isystem dirs. The existing
  build-bdx645 hermetic -I overrides were extended for the newer bundled protobuf: upb,
  upb_generator, utf8_range.h, utf8_validity.h and ares*.h now point at the bundled sources, and
  hermetic-upb holds per-file links to protobuf-src/upb/reflection/cmake (a directory symlink was
  deduplicated against the -isystem entry and lost precedence). With gRPC headers on -I, the newer
  gRPC triggers -Wdocumentation and deprecation warnings, so the build uses
  BUILD_WARNING_LEVEL=PRODUCTION instead of -Werror.
